<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Liberation Army (Algeria)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1954">1954</a>–<a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as ALN, Armée de libération nationale</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Liberation Army (ALN) was the armed wing of the Algerian FLN during the war of independence of 1954–1962. It fought a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war inside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> while large forces were held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, cut off by the fortified Morice and Challe lines. After independence it became the core of the Algerian People's National Army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-liberation-army-algeria.jpg" alt="National Liberation Army (Algeria)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Escondites · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Variant_flag_of_the_GPRA_(1958-1962).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
